    "result_text": "The full build passes (`BUILD SUCCESS`).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `membershipTier` derived field on the owner response.\n\n**Rule:** `SILVER` when `namesakeCount == 0` **and** an email is present; otherwise `BRONZE`.\n\nTwo changes, following the existing pattern used for the other computed read-only fields (`displayName`, `initials`):\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `membershipTier` string property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` includes the field.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a MapStruct `@Mapping` expression on `toOwnerDto` computing the tier:\n   ```java\n   (owner.getNamesakeCount() != null && owner.getNamesakeCount() == 0\n        && owner.getEmail() != null && !owner.getEmail().isEmpty()) ? \"SILVER\" : \"BRONZE\"\n   ```\n   The null checks guard against a null `namesakeCount`/`email` so an owner without an email (the BRONZE test case) safely falls through to `BRONZE`.\n\nThe response flows through the existing OfficeFloor `GET /api/owners/{ownerId}` pipeline (`RespondWithOwner` \u2192 `OwnerMapper.toOwnerDto`), so no YAML wiring changes were needed.\n\n**Tests:** `AcceptanceTest` (both `coreSilverWhenUniqueWithEmail` and `functionalityBronzeWhenNoEmail`) and the full suite pass \u2014 `Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`, `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
